oda</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for that classic pretzel flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">large</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">egg</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">helps give a nice golden finish</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">water</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to mix with the egg</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">coarse salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for sprinkling on top</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Filling</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">shredded cheddar cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">gooey and delicious filling</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">melted butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for brushing on top after baking</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-12249-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"12249\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Large pot&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For boiling the pretzel bites</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking sheet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For baking the pretzel bites</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Parchment paper&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">To line the baking sheet</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Slotted Spoon&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For removing the bites from boiling water</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For whisking the egg wash</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-12249-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-12249-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"12249\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat your oven to 425°F (220°C). This will ensure your pretzel bites bake perfectly!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Cut your dough into 1-inch pieces. It’s like making little doughy pillows!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Place a small amount of cheddar cheese in the center of each piece. Pinch the edges closed to form cute little bites.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bring 6 cups of water to a boil in a large pot. Stir in baking soda, then gently boil the bites for 30 seconds. This step gives them that classic pretzel texture!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Remove the bites with a slotted spoon and let them drain. Place them on a parchment-lined baking sheet.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Whisk an egg with a little water and brush it over the bites. Sprinkle with coarse salt for that extra flavor!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Bake for 12-15 minutes until they are golden brown. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12249-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Brush the warm bites with melted butter and serve immediately. Enjoy your cheesy pretzel bites!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-12249-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>10g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>6g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>24g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients for your delicious <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretzel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">pretzel </a>bites with cheese!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Pretzel-Bites-with-Cheese.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for pretzel bites with cheese displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-12247\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Pretzel-Bites-with-Cheese.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Pretzel-Bites-with-Cheese-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>1 package refrigerated pizza dough</strong> – the base for your pretzel bites</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/4 cup baking soda</strong> – for that classic pretzel flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 large egg</strong> – helps give a nice golden finish</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tbsp water</strong> – to mix with the egg</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>coarse salt</strong> – for sprinkling on top</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup shredded cheddar cheese</strong> – gooey and delicious filling</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp melted butter</strong> – for brushing on top after baking</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-pretzel-bites-with-cheese\"><strong>How to Make pretzel bites with cheese</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready for a fun and cheesy adventure! This recipe takes about 20 minutes to prepare, 12-15 minutes to cook, and an extra 30 seconds for boiling. Let’s dive in!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Making-Pretzel-Bites-with-Cheese.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making pretzel bites with cheese, including preheating the oven, preparing dough, adding cheese, and boiling the bites.\" class=\"wp-image-12248\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Making-Pretzel-Bites-with-Cheese.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Making-Pretzel-Bites-with-Cheese-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 425°F (220°C). This will ensure your pretzel bites bake perfectly!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Dough</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cut your dough into 1-inch pieces. It’s like making little doughy pillows!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add the Cheese</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place a small amount of cheddar cheese in the center of each piece. Pinch the edges closed to form cute little bites.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Boil the Bites</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bring 6 cups of water to a boil in a large pot. Stir in baking soda, then gently boil the bites for 30 seconds. This step gives them that classic pretzel texture!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Drain and Prepare for Baking</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the bites with a slotted spoon and let them drain. Place them on a parchment-lined baking sheet.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Brush and Season</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Whisk an egg with a little water and brush it over the bites. Sprinkle with coarse salt for that extra flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Bake to Perfection</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bake for 12-15 minutes until they are golden brown. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Brush the warm bites with melted butter and serve immediately. Enjoy your cheesy pretzel bites!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Snack</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>30 minutes (boiling)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>65 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm and cheesy!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-pretzel-bites-with-cheese\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making pretzel bites with cheese</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use warm water to activate the yeast for a fluffier texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t skip the baking soda bath; it gives that classic pretzel flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different cheeses for unique flavor combinations.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brush with melted butter right after baking for a golden finish.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a variety of dipping sauces for extra fun!</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-pretzel-bites-with-cheese\"><strong>How to Serve this pretzel bites with cheese</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve warm with a side of creamy ranch dip for a zesty kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a tangy mustard sauce for that classic pretzel experience.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a side of marinara sauce for a fun twist on flavors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with a sprinkle of garlic powder and fresh herbs for an extra flavor boost.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a refreshing cucumber salad for a light contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Make it a game day snack by serving with assorted dips like hummus or guacamole.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your pretzel bites with cheese later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow pretzel bites to cool completely.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place them in an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool pretzel bites completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Arrange in a single layer on a baking sheet.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for 1-2 hours, then transfer to a freezer bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label and store in the freezer for up to 2 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>For refrigerated bites, preheat oven to 350°F (175°C).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place bites on a baking sheet and cover with foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat for about 10-15 minutes until warm.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For frozen bites, add an extra 5-10 minutes to heating time.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What cheese is good for pretzel bites?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>For pretzel bites, cheeses that melt well are ideal. Cheddar, mozzarella, and Monterey Jack are popular choices. You can also experiment with a blend of cheeses for a more complex flavor. Just make sure the cheese is shredded for easy melting!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What sauce goes well with pretzel bites?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Pretzel bites pair wonderfully with a variety of sauces. Classic options include mustard, cheese sauce, or a tangy ranch dressing. For a twist, try a spicy sriracha mayo or a sweet honey mustard. The choice is yours!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How to keep pretzel bites from getting soggy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To keep your pretzel bites from getting soggy, make sure to store them in an airtight container at room temperature. If you need to reheat them, do so in the oven to maintain their crispiness. Avoid microwaving, as this can make them chewy and soggy!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Can you make pretzel bites ahead of time?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can make pretzel bites ahead of time! Prepare them as directed, then let them cool completely before storing them in an airtight container. You can reheat them in the oven when you&#8217;re ready to serve for that fresh-baked taste!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to indulge in the warm, cheesy goodness of these pretzel bites! They’re not just easy to make, but they also bring a delightful twist to your snack time. So gather your loved ones, whip up a batch, and enjoy the simple pleasure of homemade treats. You’ll be smiling with every gooey bite!</p>\n",
